Having identified the different EDSR transitions in the left 3P qubit register, we now investigate the use of controlled-SWAP gates between the electron and nuclear spins to initialize the nuclear spins by polarization transfer from the electron spin qubit. The overall nuclear spin initialization fidelity depends strongly on the efficiency of each EDSR inversion pulse, which requires a careful optimization between the EDSR power and the pulse duration using Landau–Zener interferometry (Supplementary Information III). Figure 4a shows the sequence used to determine the initialization fidelity, in this case into the \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
